  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the shelter and living conditions of the most vulnerable IDPs in Yemen through non-food items (NFIs) distributions and shelter interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the activities proposed under this project, and in coordination with other Clusters and Working Groups, the project is expected to improve the dignity, living and health conditions and protection situation of 6,215 households (estimated 43,505 individuals) IDPs in Yemen through activities under the ES/NFI sector, namely the provision of shelter solutions and NFI kits through 1) Distribution of Contingency Non-Food Items /Shelter Cluster Common Pipeline; 2) Distribution of Contingency Emergency Shelter /Shelter Cluster Common Pipeline; 3) Provision of shelter maintenance and upgrades; 4) Provision of transitional shelter; 5) Rehabilitation of houses.</narrative>
  </description>
